# Claude Code harness artifacts — transient session state, never part of a release.
.claude/ralph-loop.local.md
.claude/loop-blocked.md
.claude/settings.local.json

# Scratch body file for changelog-entry.mjs. Written at the repo root mid-release;
# an uncommitted copy would trip the loop's own dirty-tree gate (RALPH.md D3).
/entry.md

# Local development (`npm run dev`). None of this is part of a release.
#
# node_modules/ — the pinned wrangler and its runtime (workerd, esbuild). package.json and
#               package-lock.json ARE committed; the installed tree is not. `npm ci` rebuilds it.
# .wrangler/  — miniflare's local simulation state: the local D1 file, local R2 objects,
#               and caches. It is a THROWAWAY replica, never the live database. Deleting it
#               costs nothing but `npm run db:reset:local`, which rebuilds the schema from
#               worker/testkit/journey-schema.sql. (That line used to read "costs nothing but a
#               re-seed (see below)" and there was no below: nothing in the repo could rebuild a
#               local database, and the one that existed was missing ten tables.
#               worker/scripts/seed-local.mjs is now the below.)
# .dev.vars   — local values for the bindings wrangler.toml does not carry. It is the local
#               twin of `wrangler secret`, so it must never be committed even when it holds
#               only placeholders today. Real secrets stay in GitHub repo secrets (§2).
#
# All three are untracked on purpose: an uncommitted copy would trip the dirty-tree gate the
# same way /entry.md does.
node_modules/
.wrangler/
.dev.vars*
